{
  "title": "Compare transformed-text entropy at matched source length",
  "program": "J",
  "on_path": false,
  "hard": false,
  "statement": "For reversible transformations used as pseudotext controls, report held-apart model code lengths on the original symbol scale alongside per-output entropy summaries. Preserve token boundaries and include padding controls so an apparent drop can be traced to deterministic redundancy, stochastic expansion, or the finite-order model.",
  "check": "Use disjoint public training and evaluation works, verify inversion exactly, and report all orders 0–8 for identity, fixed substitution, constant letter padding, deterministic two-symbol padding, matched random two-symbol padding, and constant word suffix. Include an inverse-aware reference and both denominators.",
  "source": "Bowern and Gaskell, Character Entropy in Historical Texts: Beyond Language, CEUR Workshop Proceedings 3313 (2022), §2 and Table 1, https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3313/paper6.pdf. Related open-source catalogue https://github.com/Ayan-Bandyopadhyay/voynich-swarm/pull/423.",
  "methods": "Use the first 100 normalized blocks of each training work and the first 30 of each evaluation work from the pinned reference corpus. Compare Augustine/Erasmus, Dante/Villani, Lucanor/Buen Amor and Chaucer/Paston. Reset context at the existing block boundaries. Keep spaces, use fixed lowercase-ASCII support and reserve uppercase pad symbols. Use order 0–8 character models with recursive Dirichlet backoff of strength 2 and a 0.5 base pseudocount. For the two-symbol controls, choose B or D via parity of the preceding source letter index or independently via a coin estimated from those deterministic training pads. Fix independent train/test random seeds 40801/40802. The constant word suffix is a separate comparator. No manuscript data enter the test.",
  "findings": "The addB analogue expands source length by 1.82–1.86. For Latin, Italian, Spanish and English respectively, order-8 identity rates are 3.785, 3.969, 3.677 and 3.386 bits per source symbol. At the same order, constant B padding yields 2.163, 2.368, 2.177 and 1.964 bits per output symbol, or 4.021, 4.342, 3.965 and 3.580 per source symbol. Fixed substitution preserves every measured rate. Matched random padding also reduces the order-8 per-output rate, while costing 5.442, 5.537, 5.365 and 5.151 per source symbol. At order 4 constant padding can improve even the source-normalized estimate (Italian 3.165 vs 3.516, Spanish 3.165 vs 3.219). At the best order within 0–8, constant padding costs more per source symbol in all four pairs. Those minima describe this evaluated grid only.",
  "interpretation": "A fixed injective transformation preserves joint Shannon entropy of the whole source block. An inverse-aware encoding can model the original text and reconstruct deterministic pads for zero extra bits. Independent random pads cost the coin cross-entropy in addition to the source code. A finite-context model uses a different effective source context after insertion, so normalization alone need not make its estimates equal. This tests the denominator and transformation controls on public texts. The companion paper uses its own resampling protocol and entropy statistics.",
  "reproduction": "Save embedded python as measure.py and run PYTHONPATH=. python3 /path/to/measure.py from the project checkout with the pinned reference corpus available. It writes rates-frozen.json next to the script.",
  "python": "from collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom random import Random\nfrom string import ascii_lowercase\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\n\nfrom vs import refcorpus\n\nWORKS = {\n    \"latin\": (\"la_augustine\", \"la_erasmus\"),\n    \"italian\": (\"it_dante\", \"it_villani\"),\n    \"spanish\": (\"es_lucanor\", \"es_buenamor\"),\n    \"english\": (\"en_chaucer\", \"en_paston\"),\n}\nMAX_ORDER = 8\nALPHA = 2\nPAD = \"BD\"\nout = Path(__file__).parent\n\ndef make_options(train):\n    def deterministic(c):\n        return \"B\" if ascii_lowercase.index(c) % 2 else \"D\"\n\n    counts = Counter(deterministic(c) for line in train for c in line if c != \" \")\n    prob = counts[\"B\"] / (counts[\"B\"] + counts[\"D\"])\n    rng = Random(408)\n    letters = list(ascii_lowercase)\n    rng.shuffle(letters)\n    forward = str.maketrans(ascii_lowercase, \"\".join(letters))\n    backward = str.maketrans(\"\".join(letters), ascii_lowercase)\n    strip = str.maketrans(\"\", \"\", PAD)\n\n    def transform(line, mode, rng):\n        if mode == \"identity\":\n            return line\n        if mode == \"substitution\":\n            return line.translate(forward)\n        if mode == \"suffix_B\":\n            return \" \".join(word + \"B\" for word in line.split())\n        pieces = []\n        for c in line:\n            pieces.append(c)\n            if c == \" \":\n                continue\n            if mode == \"addB\":\n                pieces.append(\"B\")\n            elif mode == \"matched_deterministic\":\n                pieces.append(deterministic(c))\n            elif mode == \"matched_random\":\n                pieces.append(\"B\" if rng.random() < prob else \"D\")\n        return \"\".join(pieces)\n\n    def inverse(line, mode):\n        if mode == \"substitution\":\n            return line.translate(backward)\n        return line.translate(strip)\n\n    return transform, inverse, prob\n\ndef fit_score(train, test, alphabet):\n    counts = [{} for _ in range(MAX_ORDER + 1)]\n    counts[0][\"\"] = Counter()\n    for line in train:\n        for i, c in enumerate(line):\n            for k in range(min(i, MAX_ORDER) + 1):\n                key = line[i-k:i]\n                group = counts[k].get(key)\n                if group is None:\n                    group = Counter()\n                    counts[k][key] = group\n                group[c] += 1\n    totals = [{key:sum(group.values()) for key,group in col.items()} for col in counts]\n    result = [0.0] * (MAX_ORDER + 1)\n    n_symbols = 0\n    for line in test:\n        n_symbols += len(line)\n        for i, c in enumerate(line):\n            unconditional = counts[0][\"\"]\n            p = (unconditional[c] + .5) / (totals[0][\"\"] + .5 * len(alphabet))\n            for k in range(MAX_ORDER + 1):\n                if 0 < k <= i:\n                    ctx = line[i-k:i]\n                    group = counts[k].get(ctx)\n                    if group is not None:\n                        p = (group[c] + ALPHA * p) / (totals[k][ctx] + ALPHA)\n                result[k] -= math.log2(p)\n    return {\n        \"n_symbols\": n_symbols, \"total_bits\": result,\n        \"bits_per_output_symbol\": [score/n_symbols for score in result],\n    }\n\nmodes = (\"identity\", \"substitution\", \"addB\", \"matched_deterministic\", \"matched_random\", \"suffix_B\")\nresults = {}\nfor lang, (training_work, evaluation_work) in WORKS.items():\n    train = refcorpus.blocks_of(training_work)[:100]\n    test = refcorpus.blocks_of(evaluation_work)[:30]\n    assert len(train) == 100 and len(test) == 30, (lang,len(train),len(test))\n    assert not set(train) & set(test), lang\n    transform, inverse, prob = make_options(train)\n    base = sum(map(len,test))\n    row = {\n        \"works\": [training_work, evaluation_work],\n        \"n_training_source_symbols\": sum(map(len,train)), \"n_evaluation_source_symbols\": base,\n        \"source_space_count_in_evaluation\": sum(line.count(\" \") for line in test),\n        \"normalized_train_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(\"\\n\".join(train).encode()).hexdigest(),\n        \"normalized_test_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(\"\\n\".join(test).encode()).hexdigest(),\n        \"matched_padding_prob_B\": prob,\n        \"models\": {},\n    }\n    for mode in modes:\n        rng_train, rng_test = Random(40801), Random(40802)\n        cipher_train = [transform(line, mode, rng_train) for line in train]\n        cipher_test = [transform(line, mode, rng_test) for line in test]\n        assert all(inverse(line, mode) == plain for line, plain in zip(cipher_train,train))\n        assert all(inverse(line, mode) == plain for line, plain in zip(cipher_test,test))\n        assert [line.count(\" \") for line in cipher_test]==[line.count(\" \") for line in test]\n        alphabet = ascii_lowercase + \" \"\n        if mode in (\"addB\", \"suffix_B\"):\n            alphabet += \"B\"\n        elif mode in (\"matched_deterministic\", \"matched_random\"):\n            alphabet += PAD\n        measures = fit_score(cipher_train,cipher_test,alphabet)\n        measures[\"bits_per_source_symbol\"] = [score/base for score in measures[\"total_bits\"]]\n        measures[\"expansion\"] = measures[\"n_symbols\"] / base\n        if mode == \"matched_random\":\n            n_b = sum(line.count(\"B\") for line in cipher_test)\n            n_d = sum(line.count(\"D\") for line in cipher_test)\n            measures[\"structure_aware_extra_bits_per_source_symbol\"] = -(n_b*math.log2(prob)+n_d*math.log2(1-prob))/base\n        elif mode not in (\"identity\", \"substitution\"):\n            measures[\"structure_aware_extra_bits_per_source_symbol\"] = 0.0\n        row[\"models\"][mode] = measures\n    for order in range(MAX_ORDER+1):\n        assert abs(row[\"models\"][\"identity\"][\"total_bits\"][order]-row[\"models\"][\"substitution\"][\"total_bits\"][order])<1e-7\n    results[lang] = row\n    (out/\"rates-frozen.json\").write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2)+\"\\n\")\n    print(lang,row[\"n_training_source_symbols\"],row[\"n_evaluation_source_symbols\"],flush=True)\n",
